CloudBurrow patch 49 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1484). Applies after patch 0041.

The gap: a whole FLOAT64 (3.0) in a STRUCT field or an ARRAY element was
encoded with json.Marshal as the JSON integer 3, which DecodeValue (and
SQLite's json_each, under UNNEST) read back as an INT64. The analyzer
types the field FLOAT64 and adds no cast, so IntValue's arithmetic ran:
`SELECT s.x / 2 FROM (SELECT STRUCT(CAST(3 AS FLOAT64) AS x) AS s)` was 1,
s.x * 0.5 was 0 and s.x + 0.5 was 3, for a literal, a column, CAST, an
expression, a nested STRUCT, ARRAY<STRUCT>, ARRAY<FLOAT64>, a subquery's
STRUCT and a stored STRUCT column. BigQuery keeps FLOAT64, and / is
FLOAT64 for INT64 and FLOAT64 operands
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/operators#arithmetic_operators).

The patch writes a whole FLOAT64 inside an encoded STRUCT or ARRAY with a
fraction (3.0), and makes IntValue's +, - and * with a FLOAT64 operand, and
its /, FLOAT64, for a value a CloudBurrow before this patch already
stored. struct_float_test.go, TestIntValueFloatArithmetic and
TestEncodeWholeFloatInStruct fail without the patch and pass with it;
upstream's TestIntValue/Div now expects FLOAT64 5.

